1
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:35,317
I'll see you

2
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:39,360
next time.

3
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:16,620
Oh

4
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:59,488
Metal Seadramon was
blasting it into rubble!

5
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:02,437
We escaped into the ocean
on Pseudomon's back.

6
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:04,920
At least, we thought we got away.

7
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,860
Shunmoku no Kaitei, Hoeyemon!

8
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,500
What are you doing here, Diver-mon?

9
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,921
We just came up for a little air.

10
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:35,260
Those Diver-mon, if it wasn't
for their striking fish attack,

11
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,520
they'd be useless to me.

12
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,080
No matter.

13
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:41,817
Wherever those kids try
to hide, I'll find them.

14
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:45,040
I rule this ocean with an
iron hand, an iron tail,

15
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:47,457
and an iron everything for that matter.

16
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:50,820
I'll catch them even with
Whamon on their side.

17
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:53,591
Well, don't just sit there treading water.

18
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:55,820
I told you, go find those kids.

19
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:56,920
Aye, aye, sir.

20
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:10,400
Thanks for saving us, Whamon.

21
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:12,900
Don't mention it.

22
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,037
No, seriously, don't mention it.

23
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,885
I don't want it to get around.

24
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:20,000
Hey, guys, we still have a problem.

25
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:23,037
How are we going to be able
to defeat the Dark Masters?

26
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:26,317
I wonder how they took over the
digital world in the first place.

27
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:27,797
Do you remember, Whamon?

28
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:29,560
Of course I remember Whamon.

29
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:31,560
Big fella, snappy dresser.

30
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,965
Oh, you mean the Dark Masters.

31
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:38,977
I don't know all the details, but soon
after the digital world began to warp,

32
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:41,707
Metal Seadramon began
to take over the ocean.

33
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:43,720
Darn! Ow.

34
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:46,060
Oh, uh, sorry, Whamon.

35
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:48,720
Tai, don't get upset.

36
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:50,220
We'll fix things.

37
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:51,590
You're right.

38
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:52,760
We'll do it.

39
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:55,780
We've done it before, haven't we? Yeah!

40
00:03:58,260 --> 00:03:59,436
That's the attitude.

41
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:03,177
I'll find a safe place for you
outside of Meadow Sidramon's reach,

42
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:06,495
even if I have to swim to
the far corners of the ocean.

43
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:09,545
By the way, did I mention
I charge by the mile?

44
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:26,200
Can't land on their feet,
but we still need to eat.

45
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:31,240
It's Gatoman's wish for
some fresh flying fish.

46
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:34,560
Cause I'm a kitty, a digi-kitty.

47
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:48,197
That's great, Gatomom, but the
rest of us have to eat, too.

48
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:50,633
Stand aside and watch how a pro does it.

49
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:55,660
Boys and Ivy!

50
00:04:58,060 --> 00:04:58,890
Wow!

51
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,421
Dinner's served.

52
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:08,766
Why'd you stop playing, Matt?

53
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:11,616
Oh, that song is just too depressing.

54
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:13,486
It always gives me the blues.

55
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:16,956
Besides, I can't stop thinking
about the Dark Masters.

56
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:20,337
They're different than any
Digimon we've ever faced before.

57
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:25,440
Well, I've analyzed the situation, and I
believe we can defeat them with WarGreymon.

58
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,390
Huh?

59
00:05:26,473 --> 00:05:27,560
He's a Deramon Destroyer.

60
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:29,440
Deramon Destroyer?

61
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:30,840
Try speaking English.

62
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:35,120
Well, you see, the weapons on
WarGreymon's arms are the key.

63
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:39,597
They're especially effective
against Draymon-type Digimon,

64
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,739
hence the phrase Deramon Destroyer.

65
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:46,125
With these devices, we might be
able to defeat the Dark Masters.

66
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,320
Izzy, you're a genius!

67
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:49,953
Deramon Destroyer, huh?

68
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:52,927
Agumon, you're gonna
eat those Deramon alive!

69
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:01,580
That's not what I had in mind.

70
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:06,897
Hey, did you just learn
anything new in school?

71
00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:09,156
We learned diver monitor in the area.

72
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:15,880
Hey, guys, we got trouble.

73
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:20,637
I caught a whopper.

74
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:21,580
Look.

75
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:26,020
Divermon are headed this way!

76
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:28,700
Not Divermon.

77
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,037
Anything but Divermon.

78
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:31,637
By the way, what are Divermon?

79
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:34,132
Oh, those are Metal Seedramon's henchmen.

80
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:37,740
It seems the fish have seen
them about 200 miles behind us.

81
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:39,270
Huh?

82
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:41,200
What are we gonna do?

83
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,037
Well, we can't stay here.

84
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:44,497
They'll find us too easily.

85
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:45,457
I'm going to dive.

86
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:47,257
Quick, everyone get inside me.

87
00:06:47,340 --> 00:06:48,257
And don't mind the smell.

88
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:49,170
I had fish for lunch.

89
00:06:49,253 --> 00:06:50,083
Eww!

90
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:00,597
Red leader to blue leader.

91
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,560
Areas 13 through 18 are clear.

92
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:04,777
Gold leader to blue leader.

93
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:06,900
Areas 23 and 24 are clear, too.

94
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:09,857
Listen, Phil, Sid, how many
times do I have to tell you guys?

95
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:11,037
There are just three of us.

96
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:12,217
You can call me Jim!

97
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:13,177
What are you guys?

98
00:07:13,260 --> 00:07:14,500
Knock it off! Sorry!

99
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:16,237
Do you smell something?

100
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:18,237
There's a scent of
Digidestined in the current.

101
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:21,840
Either that or there's a bad
patch of seaweed around here.

102
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:24,740
This is my moment to shine!

103
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:26,257
Does my hair look all right?

104
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:27,170
Yeah!

105
00:07:27,253 --> 00:07:28,440
You Digidestined fools!

106
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:31,100
You can swim, but you can't hide!

107
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:40,659
What's that noise?

108
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,917
I was taking catnap and it woke me up.

109
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,240
I'll explain later.

110
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:45,820
Oh, come on!

111
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,471
You think I'm too brainless to understand?

112
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:50,520
Yes, but I'll tell you anyway.

113
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:53,180
Check it out!

114
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,580
What did you do, Izzy?

115
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:57,000
What a cool screensaver.

116
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,660
It's not a screensaver.

117
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:00,980
What is it, then?

118
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:03,637
I connected to Waymon's
hard drive and rerouted

119
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:06,197
all his sensory
information to my computer.

120
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:07,110
Rerouted?

121
00:08:07,193 --> 00:08:08,120
In other words,

122
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:12,497
what you're seeing on the screen is exactly
what Whamon is looking at right now.

123
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:13,980
Cool, like a submarine.

124
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:17,202
Oh, boy, I've always wanted
to go on a submarine!

125
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:20,524
I think she's been out
to sea a little too long.

126
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:23,420
Yeah, I hate square dances.

127
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:24,938
What's wrong, Kari?

128
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,100
It's my ears.

129
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:27,497
They're starting to hurt.

130
00:08:27,580 --> 00:08:28,920
Mimi, stop. Be quiet.

131
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:34,780
Oh, hey, you know, my ears
hurt a little too. Me too.

132
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:38,160
Sorry, I dove a little too fast.

133
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:40,500
I'll fix the pressure now. Hold on.

134
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,940
Oh, that's better.

135
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:51,157
Well, I guess that's one way
to equalize the gas pressure.

136
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:53,260
By the way, you're excused.

137
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:55,240
What's that sound? Huh?

138
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,640
It's getting louder.

139
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:00,260
Everyone, be quiet.

140
00:09:02,460 --> 00:09:04,020
Sounds like Divermon.

141
00:09:22,920 --> 00:09:24,780
Sounds like they've passed us.

142
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,820
We're not out of danger yet.

143
00:09:27,140 --> 00:09:29,493
You'll have to be quiet a little longer.

144
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:37,980
Over there!

145
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:39,120
Hey, it's Whamon!

146
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:44,940
Oh, no!

147
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:46,280
They found us!

148
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:05,817
Friendly, now this is...

149
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:06,837
I mean, this is Phil.

150
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:07,802
I found Whamon!

151
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:10,039
He's in Area 51 on the ocean floor!

152
00:10:13,020 --> 00:10:14,491
Great, keep an eye on it.

153
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:17,679
I'll tell the barge and he
can tell Metal Seadramon.

154
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:20,180
Good news!

155
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:21,660
We found Whamon!

156
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:23,590
Yay!

157
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:27,300
What do we do now, old
master of the ocean?

158
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:29,310
Attack!

159
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:32,360
Stacking face! Watch out!

160
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:34,148
The Divermon are attacking.

161
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:35,400
Hang on, everyone.

162
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:36,880
I've got an idea.

163
00:10:43,620 --> 00:10:45,855
Where did all those bubbles come from?

164
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:49,014
Key, I couldn't see where I was aiming.

165
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:51,220
Uh-oh.

166
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:53,360
You're squeezing me too hard.

167
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:55,699
Matt, you're squeezing me too hard.

168
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:58,212
Sorry, I guess we're all a little scared.

169
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:00,420
I hate this.

170
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:02,337
We're stuck in here and can't fight.

171
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:04,997
According to the audio
sensors, there are three more.

172
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,000
Behind us.

173
00:11:06,140 --> 00:11:07,137
What is it, Whamon?

174
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:08,102
It's the enemy.

175
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:11,472
Don't let them get away!

176
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:14,540
Oh, they're gaining on us!

177
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:15,930
That's it.

178
00:11:16,013 --> 00:11:17,215
I'm tired of running.

179
00:11:17,660 --> 00:11:20,077
Come on, Whamon, let's go
up to the surface and fight!

180
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:20,990
Right!

181
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:22,490
Well...

182
00:11:22,573 --> 00:11:23,720
Let me try one more thing.

183
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:25,400
Hopefully it'll work.

184
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:27,197
What do you mean, hopefully it'll work?

185
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:29,497
That's what the captain
of the Titanic said!

186
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:30,780
Striking fish!

187
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,997
And what if it doesn't work?

188
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:34,060
What's plan B?

189
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:36,617
I still think we should turn and fight.

190
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:39,171
I hope you know what you're doing, Whamon.

191
00:11:47,700 --> 00:11:49,080
What's he trying to do?

192
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:52,917
Whamon must be crazy trying to
escape into such a narrow space.

193
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,980
Stay with him, no matter what!

194
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:01,160
You and the big whale, pull over!

195
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:02,700
It's no use.

196
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,980
We've got your tracks. Oh, no!

197
00:12:05,380 --> 00:12:06,262
Don't catch us!

198
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:10,130
No!

199
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:13,570
No!

200
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:22,020
I'll break.

201
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:23,339
That's gotta hurt.

202
00:12:23,920 --> 00:12:24,750
Prodigious!

203
00:12:24,833 --> 00:12:26,017
They can't take the water pressure.

204
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:28,041
That was Waymon's plan all along.

205
00:12:29,060 --> 00:12:31,037
Whamon has built to handle pressure.

206
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,220
Unlike some of us.

207
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:34,854
Well, forgive me for not being a whale.

208
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:41,776
Boy, that was close.

209
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:44,437
I didn't know you had this
kind of hidden attack.

210
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:47,285
This is great, but what
are we going to do now?

211
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:50,635
Yeah, we can't stay at the
bottom of the ocean forever.

212
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:52,520
I've got it.

213
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Kari, come over here for a moment.

214
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:00,590
Right.

215
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:07,070
Ta-da!

216
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:09,470
Ready?

217
00:13:09,553 --> 00:13:10,840
You can do it!

218
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:40,700
Yeah, we did it, Kari.

219
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:44,340
Thanks for the help. Sure.

220
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:46,777
The whistle was sort of like sonar.

221
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:49,497
We used the reverberations of
the sound to find a tunnel.

222
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:51,737
And there's one up ahead
that should lead us to land.

223
00:13:51,820 --> 00:13:52,650
Come on.

224
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:54,920
Isn't that great, Whamon? What?

225
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:56,571
I said, isn't that great?

226
00:13:56,860 --> 00:13:57,860
I can't hear you.

227
00:13:58,020 --> 00:13:59,597
Someone was whistling in my ear.

228
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:01,077
But there's a tunnel up ahead.

229
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:02,689
It should lead us to land.

230
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:06,157
Those fools think I don't
know where they're headed.

231
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:09,657
They're easier to figure out
than a two-piece jigsaw puzzle.

232
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:11,975
Enjoy playing submarine while you can.

233
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:19,600
Wow, pretty!

234
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:27,460
A-ha! A tunnel? Yay!

235
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:29,420
Yay, we're safe!

236
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:31,432
I've got to get changed!

237
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:33,130
Huh?

238
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:34,710
Hug!

239
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:42,020
Not again!

240
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:43,817
How can those fish heads be back?

241
00:14:43,900 --> 00:14:44,730
They're not.

242
00:14:44,813 --> 00:14:45,757
Be careful, everyone!

243
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,220
It's Metal Seadramon!

244
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,200
Is everybody okay?

245
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:25,530
Where?

246
00:15:25,820 --> 00:15:27,160
Where are we?

247
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:31,900
The sun's so bright

248
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:37,520
Smell that, fresh air I feel
I've been underwater so long,

249
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:39,602
I might never take a bath again.

250
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:43,440
You mind telling me what's so funny?

251
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:47,515
It's Metal Seadramon!

252
00:15:47,940 --> 00:15:48,780
How can it be?

253
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:51,697
It was only a matter of time
before you came up for air.

254
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:53,898
Now you're going down with the ship!

255
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:56,080
Everyone, hold on!

256
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:01,380
Final way!

257
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:13,477
should i sure go for it
while agumon gets their

258
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:15,457
attention let's cross
over to the shore and

259
00:16:15,540 --> 00:16:19,777
prepare ourselves for
battle aye aye uh goldmaman

260
00:16:19,860 --> 00:16:22,331
and i will stay here and bring up the rear

261
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:26,257
joe don't be such a coward agumon here i

262
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:28,557
go Art of

263
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:29,977
the

264
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:37,060
Universe

265
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:38,530
Art

266
00:16:38,613 --> 00:16:45,020
of

267
00:16:56,760 --> 00:16:57,590
the

268
00:16:57,673 --> 00:16:58,503
Universe

269
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:05,389
What was that, a love tap?

270
